            <ArticleTitle>[Pudendal nerve entrapment syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>157-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Pudendal nerve entrapment syndrome is a poorly known condition and thus rarely included in our differential diagnoses. First described by Amarenco in 1987.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DEVELOPMENT" NlmCategory="METHODS">The symptomatology is varied and can be confused with other entities, in particular the pelvic floor myofascial syndrome.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The main symptom is neuropathic pain in the perineal area. The diagnosis is based on the clinical history, physical examination and the confirming neurophysiologic tests.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
